        "original_id": "d1a65ec9-0ab2-5d8a-a9e8-3d820e2d2ea7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: Blood and soil, Lebensraum\n- Organizations: Nazi Party (NSDAP), Nazi Germany\n- Places: Eastern Europe\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Blood and soil (German: \"Blut und Boden\") is a slogan expressing a nineteenth-century German idealization of a racially defined national body united with a settlement area.\n- Lebensraum is a contemporary German concept tied to blood and soil that holds that the German people needed to reclaim historically German areas of Eastern Europe for expansion.\n- The Nazi Party (NSDAP) and Nazi Germany supported the most extreme form of the Lebensraum ideology until the end of World War II.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "134191a5-194a-5589-a431-c94a2f077ae3",
        "text": "Page: Blood and Soil. Sentence: Blood and soil (German: \"Blut und Boden\" ) is a slogan expressing the nineteenth-century German idealization of a racially defined national body (\"blood\") united with a settlement area (\"soil\").\nPage: Blood and Soil. Sentence: The contemporary German concept Lebensraum, the belief that the German people needed to reclaim historically German areas of Eastern Europe into which they could expand, is tied to it.\nPage: Lebensraum. Sentence: The most extreme form of this ideology was supported by the Nazi Party (NSDAP) and Nazi Germany until the end of World War II.",
